{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349287-thallain-symbols","id":1349287,"title":"Thallain Symbols","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-17T23:05:06-08:00","id":1349287,"title":"Thallain Symbols","content":"Several years ago, I remember seeing a bunch of symbols for the various Thallain kith, and they were all sort of darker reflections of the kithain symbols. Boggans have a bee on a hexagon, but boggarts had a wasp on a pentagon. Sluagh have a spider, but Bogies had a squid. Trolls have a hammer, but Ogres had a morningstar.<br /> <br /> Low-quality example here:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/uPawm78.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> However, I can't find a source for them. Were they official? Did they come from a book? If so, which one?<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T00:03:51-08:00","id":1349294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1349287-thallain-symbols#post1349287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several years ago, I remember seeing a bunch of symbols for the various Thallain kith, and they were all sort of darker reflections of the kithain symbols. Boggans have a bee on a hexagon, but boggarts had a wasp on a pentagon. Sluagh have a spider, but Bogies had a squid. Trolls have a hammer, but Ogres had a morningstar.<br /> <br /> <br /> However, I can't find a source for them. Were they official? Did they come from a book? If so, which one?<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing in Shadow Court or Shining Host Players Guide, the primary Thallain writeups, which points to them being fan-made; if they were official, they never showed up in the major books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T04:28:12-08:00","id":1349310,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, they\u2019re a (really awesome) fan work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaK